<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">19 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 19 January, from 1419 to 1983.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/england" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1419 <span class="tih-ago">607 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rouen surrenders to Henry V</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a six-month siege that left thousands starving, Rouen yielded to Henry V of England, completing his conquest of Normandy. The Treaty of Troyes in 1420 made him heir to the French throne.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1853 <span class="tih-ago">173 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Verdi's 'Il trovatore' premieres in Rome</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Giuseppe Verdi's opera of passion and revenge opened at the Teatro Apollo to great acclaim. With 'Rigoletto' and 'La traviata', it is one of the three popular masterpieces of his middle period.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1915 <span class="tih-ago">111 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Zeppelins bomb Britain for the first time</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">German airships dropped bombs on Great Yarmouth, Sheringham and King's Lynn in Norfolk, killing four civilians. It was the first air raid on Britain, opening a new front in the war.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mexico" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mexico.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1917 <span class="tih-ago">109 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Zimmermann Telegram is forwarded to Mexico</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Germany's ambassador in Washington relayed Arthur Zimmermann's secret offer of an alliance to Mexico, promising Texas, New Mexico and Arizona. Decoded by British intelligence, its publication helped bring the US into the war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1937 <span class="tih-ago">89 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Howard Hughes sets a transcontinental air speed record</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Hughes flew his H-1 racer from Burbank, California, to Newark, New Jersey, in 7 hours, 28 minutes and 25 seconds. The record stood for seven years.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1966 <span class="tih-ago">60 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Indira Gandhi chosen to lead India</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Congress parliamentary party elected Indira Gandhi as its leader after the sudden death of Lal Bahadur Shastri. Sworn in five days later, she became India's first and only woman prime minister.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1983 <span class="tih-ago">43 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Apple announces the Lisa computer</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Apple unveiled the Lisa, a personal computer with a graphical interface and a mouse. At nearly 10,000 dollars it sold poorly, but its ideas fed directly into the Macintosh a year later.</p></div></li></ol>
